WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:03.115
An existing AHV cluster needs a rebuild.

00:00:03.456 --> 00:00:07.296
In this simulated recovery, we’ll use a recovery profile to take

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:11.190
one cluster from its saved build plan to workload restore handoff.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:14.158
Before creating the profile, verify the approved

00:00:14.286 --> 00:00:17.891
node serials, network settings, and image checksums.

00:00:18.211 --> 00:00:20.558
Save the Foundation VM deployment file and

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.105
a post-configuration pipeline for the same cluster.

00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:26.463
Open Disaster Recovery, add the datacenter, and record

00:00:26.676 --> 00:00:29.634
the Foundation VM endpoint and dependency reviews.

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:34.262
Choose Create Recovery Profile and select Existing cluster to rebuild.

00:00:34.553 --> 00:00:38.457
Link the saved deployment file and pipeline, then save the draft.

00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:42.361
Open Review Profile, check the target nodes, cluster address

00:00:42.532 --> 00:00:45.913
and captured steps, and select Mark Baseline Reviewed.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.408
If the source changes, capture and review a new revision.

00:00:49.892 --> 00:00:51.406
Select Prepare Recovery.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.732
Request deployment approval and have a second

00:00:53.902 --> 00:00:56.751
administrator approve the exact run in Approvals.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.131
Back in the recovery run, enter both

00:00:59.216 --> 00:01:02.331
confirmation phrases and acknowledge the imaging risk.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.787
Select Deploy Reviewed Recovery, then follow the linked

00:01:05.872 --> 00:01:09.247
Foundation job until imaging and cluster formation succeed.

00:01:09.596 --> 00:01:13.350
After Foundation succeeds, run initial access bootstrap if

00:01:13.393 --> 00:01:16.316
the captured pipeline includes eligible first steps.

00:01:16.635 --> 00:01:19.494
Use separate approvals where required, then run the

00:01:19.537 --> 00:01:22.362
approved password and EULA or Pulse actions.

00:01:22.797 --> 00:01:25.827
Verify the replacement credential before broader configuration.

00:01:26.253 --> 00:01:28.643
Select Collect PE Health Readbacks.

00:01:28.899 --> 00:01:31.757
Confirm the expected cluster identity, complete host

00:01:31.885 --> 00:01:34.671
membership, and health reported by Prism Element.

00:01:34.981 --> 00:01:38.757
Resolve any certificate or access error, then collect again.

00:01:38.992 --> 00:01:42.477
Start the remaining pipeline within fifteen minutes of fresh evidence.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.295
Select Run Remaining Pipeline Steps.

00:01:45.625 --> 00:01:50.553
Watch the saved DNS, time, network and storage settings run in order.

00:01:50.873 --> 00:01:53.070
Each completed step has a linked job.

00:01:53.305 --> 00:01:56.377
If a step fails, reconcile actual state and

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.180
resume unfinished work after fresh health evidence.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.366
If policy requires a separate approval, run the

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:05.524
approved step directly and link its successful job.

00:02:05.951 --> 00:02:09.442
Read back the requested settings and check current cluster health.

00:02:09.691 --> 00:02:12.635
Enter verification notes and an evidence reference,

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:15.728
then select Accept for Restore Handoff.

00:02:16.134 --> 00:02:18.651
The backup team now has the rebuilt cluster and

00:02:18.694 --> 00:02:21.878
the recovery evidence it needs to begin restoring workloads.
